      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MISS JECKELL (4) doesn't have the best strike-rate. Finished in the minors latest when second (31.22) at Ballarat and may be close to breaking through. Makes plenty of appeal. SALT SPECKLE (2) showed blistering pace early and gave a sight when in the minors, beaten one length over 500m Bendigo in 28.38. Leading player again. FRANKY'S OUTLAW (1) hit the ground running from out wide with a fast early sectional but run over late and missed the frame when a 2.75 lengths fifth (28.49) over 500m at Bendigo. Has a strong record out of this box with three wins and a minor placing from five starts. A big run wouldn't surprise. MORAINE PIPER (8) has top-three aspirations after placing at big odds last time.",
